BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Istanbul//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Istanbul — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Simit — The sesame bread ring\, dipped in grape molasses before the seeds go on — that is the dark lacquer.
DESCRIPTION:Say: see-MEET Ottoman price registers had it in Istanbul by 1525\; the state fixed its weight by decree because too many people lived off it. Best: Off the tray on the Eminönü–Kadıköy vapur
LOCATION:Off the tray on the Eminönü–Kadıköy vapur
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Emin%C3%B6n%C3%BC%20Ferry%20Pier%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Serpme kahvaltı — The sprawled Sunday breakfast — twenty small plates\, three hours\, tables held rather than turned. You get to taste everything at once.
DESCRIPTION:Say: SERP-meh kah-vahl-TUH Kahvaltı means "before coffee": the biggest meal of the Turkish day is named for the drink it precedes. Best: Van Kahvaltı Evi\, Cihangir — Sunday\, go early
LOCATION:Van Kahvaltı Evi\, Cihangir — Sunday\, go early
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Van%20Kahvalt%C4%B1%20Evi%20Cihangir%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Muhammara — Walnuts\, red-pepper paste and pomegranate molasses pounded into a coarse paste — on the breakfast spread and the meze tray both.
DESCRIPTION:Say: moo-hahm-mah-RAH The Hatay–Aleppo table in one bowl: the south-eastern half of the city's cooking\, spread on bread before nine in the morning. Best: On the serpme spread\, or at an Antakya house — Hatay Medeniyetler Sofrası
LOCATION:On the serpme spread\, or at an Antakya house — Hatay Medeniyetler Sofrası
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hatay%20Medeniyetler%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Menemen — Eggs scrambled loosely into tomato and green pepper\, eaten from the pan with bread — the Turkish cousin of shakshuka.
DESCRIPTION:Say: meh-neh-MEN Turkey's great breakfast argument: with onion or without (soğanlı / soğansız) genuinely divides the country. Order it and take a side. Best: Çakmak Kahvaltı Salonu\, Beşiktaş
LOCATION:Çakmak Kahvaltı Salonu\, Beşiktaş
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C3%87akmak%20Kahvalt%C4%B1%20Salonu%20Be%C5%9Fikta%C5%9F%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Yaprak sarma — Vine leaves rolled thin as a finger around rice\, herbs and spice\, eaten cold with a squeeze of lemon. The good ones\, mind — hand-rolled\, tight\, no shortcuts.
DESCRIPTION:Say: yah-PRAHK sahr-MAH The zeytinyağlı register — the palace half of the table: vegetables cooked in olive oil and served cold\, restraint as a cuisine. Best: The zeytinyağlı trays at Çiya Sofrası\, Kadıköy
LOCATION:The zeytinyağlı trays at Çiya Sofrası\, Kadıköy
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C3%87iya%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mercimek çorbası — Red lentil soup — and the ritual matters: fresh lemon squeezed in\, pul biber on top. Never skip either.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mehr-jee-MEK chor-bah-SUH The most democratic dish in Turkey: every lokanta opens with it\, every taxi driver has an opinion on it\, and it costs almost nothing. Best: Yanyalı Fehmi Lokantası\, Kadıköy — trading since 1919
LOCATION:Yanyalı Fehmi Lokantası\, Kadıköy — trading since 1919
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yanyal%C4%B1%20Fehmi%20Lokantas%C4%B1%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Balık ekmek — Grilled fish in a half loaf\, eaten standing by the water.
DESCRIPTION:Say: bah-LUHK ek-MEK No inventor and no founding date — it is what happens when a fishing fleet ties up at the foot of a hungry city. Best: The Karaköy waterfront counters — not the painted Eminönü boats
LOCATION:The Karaköy waterfront counters — not the painted Eminönü boats
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=bal%C4%B1k%20ekmek%20Karak%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Turşu — the pickles — Cucumber\, cabbage\, beet\, green plum — pickled sharp\, sold from barrels\, the brine drunk by the glass as turşu suyu.
DESCRIPTION:Say: toor-SHOO The turşucu is a shop that sells nothing else\, and has not needed to for a century. Drink the juice: it is the point. Best: A turşucu in the Kadıköy çarşı
LOCATION:A turşucu in the Kadıköy çarşı
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=tur%C5%9Fucu%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ayran — Salted yoghurt whipped thin\, best from the churn (yayık) with a collar of foam.
DESCRIPTION:Say: eye-RAHN A confession: the house hates it. It is still a must — no kebab is complete without the glass beside it\, and Turkey drinks more of it than anything else. Best: From the yayık wherever you sit at a fire — Tam Ocakbaşı
LOCATION:From the yayık wherever you sit at a fire — Tam Ocakbaşı
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tam%20Ocakba%C5%9F%C4%B1%20Arnavutk%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Midye dolma — Mussels stuffed with spiced rice\, sold from trays after dark\, one lemon squeeze per shell.
DESCRIPTION:Say: MEED-yeh DOHL-mah An Armenian dish before it was an Istanbul one — recorded in an 1888 yearbook\, made with large mussels and sheep-tail fat. Best: Midyeci Ahmet\, Beşiktaş çarşı
LOCATION:Midyeci Ahmet\, Beşiktaş çarşı
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Midyeci%20Ahmet%20Karak%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ciğer at the ocakbaşı — Liver first\, then the skewers\, a lahmacun to close — you sit at the charcoal trench and the cook works in front of you.
DESCRIPTION:Say: jee-EHR at the oh-jak-bah-SHUH The most Istanbul way to eat fire: the ocakbaşı is a bar with a grill in it\, carried north by south-eastern migration. Best: Tam Ocakbaşı\, Arnavutköy — book for Friday or Saturday
LOCATION:Tam Ocakbaşı\, Arnavutköy — book for Friday or Saturday
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tam%20Ocakba%C5%9F%C4%B1%20Arnavutk%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Fıstıklı kuru baklava — The dry pistachio baklava — no cream\, cut small\, bought by weight.
DESCRIPTION:Say: fuhs-tuhk-LUH koo-ROO bahk-lah-VAH The Güllü family carried the craft from Damascus to Gaziantep in 1871\; the dry version survives being carried onto a boat. Best: Karaköy Güllüoğlu — open past midnight
LOCATION:Karaköy Güllüoğlu — open past midnight
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Karak%C3%B6y%20G%C3%BCll%C3%BCo%C4%9Flu%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Künefe — Shredded pastry over molten cheese\, cooked to order and eaten hot — it does not wait for you.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kew-neh-FEH Antakya's dessert\, made properly in Istanbul by houses that came north from Hatay. Best: Hatay Medeniyetler Sofrası\, off İstiklal
LOCATION:Hatay Medeniyetler Sofrası\, off İstiklal
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hatay%20Medeniyetler%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Boza — Fermented millet\, thick and faintly sour\, with cinnamon and roasted chickpeas on top. Winter only — it spoils in heat.
DESCRIPTION:Say: BOH-zah Vefa Bozacısı has poured it since 1876 in a room that has barely changed\; the only shop of its generation still trading. Best: Vefa Bozacısı\, Fatih
LOCATION:Vefa Bozacısı\, Fatih
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Vefa%20Bozac%C4%B1s%C4%B1%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Türk kahvesi — Coffee milled finer than espresso\, brought up slowly in the cezve and never allowed to boil — judge it by the foam.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tewrk kah-veh-SEE The word kahvaltı itself bows to this cup: everything eaten before it is just preparation. Best: Fazıl Bey\, Kadıköy çarşı
LOCATION:Fazıl Bey\, Kadıköy çarşı
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Faz%C4%B1l%20Bey%20T%C3%BCrk%20Kahvesi%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Çay on the ferry deck — Tea in a tulip glass from the tray that never spills\, on the open deck mid-strait.
DESCRIPTION:Say: CHAI Twenty minutes\, the price of a bus ride\, and the best view in the city is included. Best: Any Şehir Hatları vapur — take the aft deck
LOCATION:Any Şehir Hatları vapur — take the aft deck
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Emin%C3%B6n%C3%BC%20Ferry%20Pier%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Rakı-balık — The full meyhane night: cold mezes\, then hot\, then one fish — chosen off the ice by the door and weighed in front of you\, never off a menu.
DESCRIPTION:Say: rah-KUH bah-LUHK The meyhane table was built by the city's Greeks\, Armenians and Jews\; the ritual outlived its authors. Best: Agora Meyhanesi 1890\, Balat
LOCATION:Agora Meyhanesi 1890\, Balat
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Agora%20Meyhanesi%201890%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-18@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tavuk göğsü — A milk pudding thickened with chicken breast pulled so fine you cannot find it — sweet\, not savoury.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tah-VOOK goess-SUE A palace dessert a patisserie cannot make\; order it where a muhallebici still exists to make it. Best: Saray Muhallebicisi\, İstiklal
LOCATION:Saray Muhallebicisi\, İstiklal
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Saray%20Muhallebicisi%20%C4%B0stiklal%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-19@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:İşkembe soup — Tripe soup\, garlic vinegar on top\, taken after midnight against the rakı.
DESCRIPTION:Say: eesh-kem-BEH The city's licensed cure: işkembeci keep the hours the meyhane makes necessary. Best: Lale İşkembecisi\, Tarlabaşı — since 1965
LOCATION:Lale İşkembecisi\, Tarlabaşı — since 1965
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lale%20%C4%B0%C5%9Fkembecisi%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-20@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Öküzgözü — The juicy\, dark-fruited Anatolian red — the name means "ox eye"\, after the size of the berries.
DESCRIPTION:Say: oh-kooz-goh-ZOO One of the indigenous grapes almost nobody outside Turkey orders — which is exactly why to order it here. Best: Solera Winery\, Tomtom
LOCATION:Solera Winery\, Tomtom
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Solera%20Winery%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-21@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Boğazkere — The tannic Anatolian red — the name means "throat burner". Built for lamb off the fire.
DESCRIPTION:Say: boh-ahz-keh-REH Drink it at an ocakbaşı and the pairing explains both the grape and the grill. Best: Sensus Wine Boutique\, Galata
LOCATION:Sensus Wine Boutique\, Galata
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sensus%20Wine%20Boutique%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:istanbul-liste-22@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Narince & Emir — The Anatolian whites\, cold: Narince from Tokat\, Emir from Cappadocia.
DESCRIPTION:Say: nah-rin-DJEH · eh-MEER Grown on some of the oldest wine ground on earth\, and still barely exported. Best: WAYANA Wine Bar\, Moda\, Kadıköy
LOCATION:WAYANA Wine Bar\, Moda\, Kadıköy
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=WAYANA%20Wine%20Bar%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
